module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.bare_reference_closure_widens_to_the_corpus

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data bare_reference_closure_widens_to_the_corpus: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "bare_reference_closure_widens_to_the_corpus" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "bare-reference closure widens to the corpus (the seed's entry closure, v1_compiler.cli_run extend_sources_to_both_closure_fixpoint, admits a module into an entry's closure when it DECLARES a name the entry spells bare, so a common spelling pulls in every declarer and each pulled module's bare names pull in more; the reported symptom was ~the whole corpus; the measured closure for this entry on main da5a327d69 is 547 modules, still including v2.compiler.parse, v2.compiler.tokenize, v2.extdeps.languages.python and v2.std.grammar, which a git ref transition does not depend on -- the edge pulling them is not yet attributed).",
    "INVALID STATE: a closure that contains modules the entry does not depend on -- membership decided by spelling coincidence rather than by the resolved binding. HARM: every consumer of the closure pays for modules it does not use; receipt srv1 run 36032847731, gunbc-tree-sync.service spent 38 min wall (4 min CPU) resolving a small convergence entry, reclaim-throttled at 27.9G; the same compile measured in a session container is 299s wall and 10.0 GiB peak RSS.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the closure contains compiler and language modules unrelated to the entry's subject; admit_pool_bare_references scans every import-free module in the pool regardless of the entry.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (TimeoutStartSec, gunbc#12246, only bounds the harm). CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- a closure edge that is the resolved binding of a reference, not a name match, is decidable and fully modeled once binding precedes closure. NEXT TRIGGER: closure membership derived from resolved occurrence bindings (std.occurrence_identity) rather than a bare-name census. Not fixed here: the convergence lane removes this consumer by emitting the program ahead of the host (option b); the root cause is left for a later lane.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
